# Municipal Services Application — Part 1 (Report Issues)

PROG7312 / AAPD7112 — Programming 3B: Advanced Application Development
C# .NET Framework (net472) Windows Forms application.

## How to Compile and Run

### Requirements
- Windows 10/11
- Visual Studio 2022 (Community edition is free) with the
  **.NET desktop development** workload installed
- .NET Framework 4.7.2 Developer Pack (Visual Studio installer will
  prompt you to add this automatically if it's missing)

### Steps
1. Copy the whole `MunicipalServicesApp` folder onto the Windows machine.
2. Double-click `MunicipalServicesApp.sln` to open it in Visual Studio.
   (If prompted to install a missing targeting pack, accept — Visual
   Studio will fetch the net472 reference assemblies automatically.)
3. Press **F5** (or Build → Build Solution, then Debug → Start Without
   Debugging) to compile and run.
4. The Main Menu window should appear.

No NuGet packages are required — the project only uses the built-in
`System.Windows.Forms` and `System.Drawing` assemblies that ship with
.NET Framework.

## How to Use

1. **Main Menu** opens on startup with three options:
   - **Report Issues** — fully implemented, click to open.
   - **Local Events and Announcements** — disabled (implemented in Part 2).
   - **Service Request Status** — disabled (implemented in the PoE / Part 3).

2. **Report Issues**:
   - Enter the **Location** of the issue.
   - Select a **Category** (Sanitation, Roads, Water and Sewage,
     Electricity, Utilities, Other).
   - Type a **Description** in the rich text box.
   - Optionally click **Attach Image / Document...** to attach a
     supporting file via the file picker.
   - As you fill in each field, the **progress bar and message below
     the form update in real time** — this is the user engagement
     strategy (real-time feedback / status-tracking) chosen and
     justified in the Task 1 research document.
   - Click **Submit**. You'll receive a confirmation with a reference
     number. The form then clears so you can report another issue.
   - Click **Back to Main Menu** at any time to return.

## Architecture Notes

- `Models/Issue.cs` — the data model for a single reported issue
  (location, category, description, attachment path, timestamp, status).
- `Models/IssueRepository.cs` — an in-memory `List<Issue>` used to store
  every issue reported during the session (Technical Requirement: use
  an appropriate data structure to store user-reported issues). This
  repository is intentionally kept simple and static so that Part 2 and
  the PoE can build additional features (events, service-request
  tracking) on top of the same underlying issue data.
- `Forms/MainMenuForm.cs` — the startup menu, with only "Report Issues"
  enabled as required.
- `Forms/ReportIssueForm.cs` — the Report Issues window: all UI controls
  required by the brief (location textbox, category dropdown,
  description RichTextBox, OpenFileDialog-based attachment button,
  submit button, engagement ProgressBar/label, back button), plus input
  validation and the live engagement feature.

## Known Limitations (Part 1 scope)

- Local Events and Service Request Status are intentionally disabled;
  they are out of scope for Part 1 and will be implemented in Part 2
  and the PoE respectively.
- Issue data is held in memory only and is not persisted between runs
  of the application, since no persistence requirement is specified
  for Part 1.

